<!--
    C++ anonymous namespaces survive the name-only demangling (and the
    `symbolnamerepair` backstop behind them).

    Itanium mangles an anonymous namespace as `_GLOBAL__N_...` and the demangler
    renders it `(anonymous namespace)`. The name-only reduction strips every
    balanced bracket group, so it used to delete that component WHOLE and leave
    an empty `::` piece: `outer::(anonymous namespace)::nested_helper` became
    `outer::::nested_helper`. The scope splitter
    (`Database::find_create_scope_from_symbol_name`) nests one Scope per `::`
    component and `attach_scope` rejects an empty one; because the symbol table
    is installed inside `load file`, that error escaped the architecture build
    entirely, so EVERY command on such a binary answered `could not build an
    architecture ... Non-global scope has empty name` and emitted nothing.

    An anonymous namespace is the ordinary way C++ gives a definition internal
    linkage, so this was most unstripped C++, not an exotic input.

    The XML wrapper only supplies the harness architecture; the script clears it
    and loads a real x86-64 C++ ELF fixture built by g++ -O1, whose source
    (`anon_namespace_x86_64.cpp`) carries the three shapes that mattered: an
    anonymous namespace nested inside a named one, a class defined inside that
    one, and a top-level anonymous namespace (the leading-`::` case).

    This is the DEFAULT/fixed arm only, and deliberately so. The paired broken
    arm cannot be a second pass here: the bug is a LOAD failure, and `option`
    requires a live image, so the gate that restores it (`symbolnamerepair off`)
    has to be set before `load file` through its env bridge, which no script
    command can do. The regression signal is still loud rather than silent: a failed `load
    file` makes every later command error the script out, the file applies 0
    assertions, and the baseline comparison reports REGRESSED. The option's own
    two-pass on/off coverage lives in the Rust gate
    `decompiler/crates/kuna-console/tests/verify_symbolnamerepair.rs`, which can
    set the env var around each load.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/anon_namespace_x86_64</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>load function anonymous_namespace::top_helper</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load function outer::anonymous_namespace::nested_helper</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>load function outer::anonymous_namespace::Widget::emit</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
